  "kind": "recipe",
  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "standard",
    "description": "tonyd2wild's DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp (native image input, bundled DSpark draft head) on two Sparks with SGLang tensor parallel 2 over RoCE, from the SGLang DeepSeek-V4 cookbook's verified dgx-spark flash-vision fp4 balanced cell: b12x MoE runner, DSpark speculative decoding, 327,680-token context, about a 507K-token KV pool, thinking off by default. Image: the SGLang DGX Spark preview build lmsysorg/sglang:dev-v4f-2dgx-v2 (branch b12x-vision @ 452239a74f), pinned by digest and used unmodified. Upstream calls this a staging checkpoint: untuned, the DSpark accept length observed was 1.7 to 2.6 tokens per step, and the TP4 lane is only planned (not packaged). Same-creator alternative for this model and Spark count: the vLLM DSpark recipe. Host prerequisite from upstream: the FP8-to-FP4 weight conversion needs tens of GB of host memory on GB10, so upstream adds a 48 GB swapfile per node as a safety net (peak swap use about 36 GB). Licences (information only): recipe MIT, model MIT, SGLang Apache-2.0. Upstream figures (about 45 tok/s median real-prompt single stream, 75 tok/s aggregate at 16 streams) are claims until measured here; Vonk physical two-Spark acceptance is pending. Thinking default is chosen per request (chat template kwargs or sampling parameters), not as a recipe option; server default: Thinking off unless a request enables it (upstream default).",
